as output by\n 83 |         'utils.multiclass.type_of_target'.\n 84 | \n 85 |     y_true : array-like of shape (n_samples, n_outputs)\n 86 |         Ground truth (correct) target values.\n 87 | \n 88 |     y_pred : array-like of shape (n_samples, n_outputs)\n 89 |         Estimated target values.\n 90 | \n 91 |     multioutput : array-like of shape (n_outputs) or string in ['raw_values',\n 92 |         uniform_average', 'variance_weighted'] or None\n 93 |         Custom output weights if ``multioutput`` is array-like or\n 94 |         just the corresponding argument if ``multioutput`` is a\n 95 |         correct keyword.\n 96 |     \"\"\"\n 97 |     xp, _ = get_namespace(y_true, y_pred, multioutput, xp=xp)\n 98 | \n 99 |     check_consistent_length(y_true, y_pred)\n100 |     y_true = check_array(y_true, ensure_2d=False, dtype=dtype)\n101 |     y_pred = check_array(y_pred, ensure_2d=False, dtype=dtype)\n102 | \n103 |     if y_true.ndim == 1:\n104 |         y_true = xp.reshape(y_true, (-1, 1))\n105 | \n106 |     if y_pred.ndim == 1:\n107 |         y_pred = xp.reshape(y_pred, (-1, 1))\n108 | \n109 |     if y_true.shape[1] != y_pred.shape[1]:\n110 |         raise ValueError(\n111 |             \"y_true and y_pred have different number of output ({0}!={1})\".format(\n112 |                 y_true.shape[1], y_pred.shape[1]\n113 |             )\n114 |         )\n115 | \n116 |     n_outputs = y_true.shape[1]\n117 |     allowed_multioutput_str = (\"raw_values\", \"uniform_average\", \"variance_weighted\")\n118 |     if isinstance(multioutput, str):\n119 |         if multioutput not in allowed_multioutput_str:\n120 |             raise ValueError(\n121 |                 \"Allowed 'multioutput' string values are {}. \"\n122 |                 \"You provided multioutput={!r}\".format(\n123 |                     allowed_multioutput_str, multioutput\n124 |                 )\n125 |             )\n126 |     elif multioutput is not None:\n127 |         multioutput = check_array(multiou