s 1652-1660) which handles the conversion of input segments into internal Path objects, confirming the requested format can be implemented.\n\n4. `_add_data_doc` in matplotlib/_docstring.py (lines 1403-1444) which handles data parameter documentation, showing how data-related docstrings are processed in Matplotlib.\n\n5. `Artist._update_set_signature_and_docstring` in matplotlib/artist.py (lines 159-172) which handles the automatic generation of docstring signatures, ensuring the changes won't break this functionality.\n\nThese locations represent the complete chain of code that handles the LineCollection's docstring and implementation, covering both the public interface and internal data processing.", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "user", "content": "Verify if the found locations contain all the necessary information to address the issue, and check for any relevant references in other parts of the codebase that may not have appeared in the search results. If not, continue searching for additional locations related to the issue.\nVerify that you have carefully analyzed the impact of the found locations on the repository, especially their dependencies. If you think you have solved the task, rewrite your final answer into the required location-only format, output ONLY the location block, and then call `finish` to finish.\nIMPORTANT: YOU SHOULD NEVER ASK FOR HUMAN HELP.\nDaLIC raw evidence tools remain available throughout the investigation.\nIf your current evidence is either too broad, too few or incomplete, call `get_trace_artifacts` again with more precise filters before finishing.\n"}, {"content": "Let me verify the completeness of the found locations by checking additional dependencies and references.\n\nFirst, let's explore the dependencies of LineCollection:\n\n<function=explore_tree_structure>\n<parameter=start_entities>['lib/matplotlib/collections.py:LineCollection']</parameter>\n<parameter=direction>both</parameter