l_reference(self, key: Level, axis: Axis = 0) -> bool:\n1590 |         \"\"\"\n1591 |         Test whether a key is a level reference for a given axis.\n1592 | \n1593 |         To be considered a level reference, `key` must be a string that:\n1594 |           - (axis=0): Matches the name of an index level and does NOT match\n1595 |             a column label.\n1596 |           - (axis=1): Matches the name of a column level and does NOT match\n1597 |             an index label.\n1598 | \n1599 |         Parameters\n1600 |         ----------\n1601 |         key : Hashable\n1602 |             Potential level name for the given axis\n1603 |         axis : int, default 0\n1604 |             Axis that levels are associated with (0 for index, 1 for columns)\n1605 | \n1606 |         Returns\n1607 |         -------\n1608 |         is_level : bool\n1609 |         \"\"\"\n1610 |         axis_int = self._get_axis_number(axis)\n1611 | \n1612 |         return (\n1613 |             key is not None\n1614 |             and is_hashable(key)\n1615 |             and key in self.axes[axis_int].names\n1616 |             and not self._is_label_reference(key, axis=axis_int)\n1617 |         )\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/core/generic.py:NDFrame._is_label_reference`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n1620 | def _is_label_reference(self, key: Level, axis: Axis = 0) -> bool:\n1621 |         \"\"\"\n1622 |         Test whether a key is a label reference for a given axis.\n1623 | \n1624 |         To be considered a label reference, `key` must be a string that:\n1625 |           - (axis=0): Matches a column label\n1626 |           - (axis=1): Matches an index label\n1627 | \n1628 |         Parameters\n1629 |         ----------\n1630 |         key : Hashable\n1631 |             Potential label name, i.e. Index entry.\n1632 |         axis : int, default 0\n1633 |             Axis perpendicular to the axis that labels are associated with\n1634 |             (0 means