at it matches both a level of the input\n1680 |         `axis` and a label of the other axis.\n1681 | \n1682 |         Parameters\n1683 |         ----------\n1684 |         key : Hashable\n1685 |             Label or level name.\n1686 |         axis : int, default 0\n1687 |             Axis that levels are associated with (0 for index, 1 for columns).\n1688 | \n1689 |         Raises\n1690 |         ------\n1691 |         ValueError: `key` is ambiguous\n1692 |         \"\"\"\n1693 | \n1694 |         axis_int = self._get_axis_number(axis)\n1695 |         other_axes = (ax for ax in range(self._AXIS_LEN) if ax != axis_int)\n1696 | \n1697 |         if (\n1698 |             key is not None\n1699 |             and is_hashable(key)\n1700 |             and key in self.axes[axis_int].names\n1701 |             and any(key in self.axes[ax] for ax in other_axes)\n1702 |         ):\n1703 |             # Build an informative and grammatical warning\n1704 |             level_article, level_type = (\n1705 |                 (\"an\", \"index\") if axis_int == 0 else (\"a\", \"column\")\n1706 |             )\n1707 | \n1708 |             label_article, label_type = (\n1709 |                 (\"a\", \"column\") if axis_int == 0 else (\"an\", \"index\")\n1710 |             )\n1711 | \n1712 |             msg = (\n1713 |                 f\"'{key}' is both {level_article} {level_type} level and \"\n1714 |                 f\"{label_article} {label_type} label, which is ambiguous.\"\n1715 |             )\n1716 |             raise ValueError(msg)\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/core/generic.py:NDFrame._get_label_or_level_values`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n1719 | def _get_label_or_level_values(self, key: Level, axis: AxisInt = 0) -> ArrayLike:\n1720 |         \"\"\"\n1721 |         Return a 1-D array of values associated with `key`, a label or level\n1722 |         from the given `axis`.\n1723 | \n1724 |         Retrieval logic:\n1725 |           - (axis=0